2026-10-23T10:10:58.2367152Z Linux USB/IP device management (experimental preview)
2026-10-23T10:10:58.2367566Z 
2026-10-23T10:10:58.2367693Z Usage: rustusb [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>
2026-10-23T10:10:58.2367917Z 
2026-10-23T10:10:58.2368003Z Commands:
2026-10-23T10:10:58.2368542Z   physical-pending    Inspect unresolved physical grants through the root helper (root only)
2026-10-23T10:10:58.2369255Z   physical-reconcile  Verify restored physical state and retire its grant record (root only; no USB writes)
2026-10-23T10:10:58.2370287Z   physical-server     Serve explicitly authorized whole USB devices through Linux USBFS (experimental, no TLS)
2026-10-23T10:10:58.2371074Z   virtual-server      Serve two virtual test devices; this experimental mode provides no authentication or TLS
2026-10-23T10:10:58.2371822Z   devices             Scan local devices without changing drivers. Discovery is not compatibility validation
2026-10-23T10:10:58.2372495Z   doctor              Read installed tool, module and helper capabilities without loading modules
2026-10-23T10:10:58.2373110Z   discover            Query a server's USB/IP device list over an administrator-managed trusted network
2026-10-23T10:10:58.2373795Z   export              Export an administrator-allowlisted device fingerprint via the privileged helper
2026-10-23T10:10:58.2374759Z   unexport            Release an allowlisted export and request local driver reattachment
2026-10-23T10:10:58.2375369Z   attach              Import a remote bus ID through an allowlisted endpoint and Linux VHCI
2026-10-23T10:10:58.2375901Z   detach              Disconnect an authorized local VHCI port (0..255)
2026-10-23T10:10:58.2376383Z   sessions            Read authoritative native kernel session state through the helper
2026-10-23T10:10:58.2377248Z   status              Query helper and kernel status
2026-10-23T10:10:58.2377657Z   help                Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
2026-10-23T10:10:58.2377950Z 
2026-10-23T10:10:58.2378022Z Options:
